<%# The order-sound control, rendered wherever the pending badge is: the
    sidebar, and the mobile top bar, which is the only one of the two a phone
    shows without opening the drawer. Same reasoning, same pair of ids.

    All three faces are in the markup at once and the stylesheet shows one of
    them, keyed off data-sound-state. The state is written by
    order_sound_controller.js, which never builds markup or assembles a class
    name — Tailwind only emits rules for literal strings it can find in these
    files, so anything stitched together at runtime would silently get no CSS.

    display:none takes the two inactive faces out of the accessibility tree as
    well as out of the layout, so the button's accessible name is whichever one
    is showing. That is deliberate: it is the state the label has to carry,
    which is why aria-pressed alone is not enough here. There are three states
    and aria-pressed only has two useful values — "blocked" (the owner asked
    for sound, the browser has not granted this document audio yet) reports
    aria-pressed="false", because no sound would in fact be made, and says so
    in words instead.

    `class_name` and `label_class` are passed whole from the call sites rather
    than built here, for the same Tailwind reason. %>
<button type="button"
        id="<%= id %>"
        class="<%= class_name %>"
        data-order-sound-target="toggle"
        data-action="order-sound#toggle"
        data-sound-state="off"
        aria-pressed="false">
  <span class="sound-face sound-face-on">
    <%= icon "speaker-simple-high", class: "size-4 shrink-0" %>
    <span class="<%= label_class %>"><%= t("owner.orders.sound.enabled") %></span>
  </span>
  <span class="sound-face sound-face-off">
    <%= icon "speaker-simple-slash", class: "size-4 shrink-0" %>
    <span class="<%= label_class %>"><%= t("owner.orders.sound.disabled") %></span>
  </span>
  <span class="sound-face sound-face-blocked">
    <%= icon "speaker-simple-x", class: "size-4 shrink-0" %>
    <span class="<%= label_class %>"><%= t("owner.orders.sound.blocked") %></span>
  </span>
</button>
